    "interpretation": "If the 4 backbones are placed side-by-side (⊗ = monoidal product), the strongest one carries the system → ⊤ = ⊤_pub. But if they are integrated into a cross-border system (▷ = cospan-pushout), the weakest one drags the rest down → ⊥' = ⊤_priv. Same set, different composition direction, different bottleneck. (notes/15 Theorem: Bottleneck Reversal)"
  },
  "interpretation": {
    "trust_gap": "4 backbone types reach different Heyting upper bounds: Bakong (central bank) → ⊤_pub, PayNow & KBZPay (bank) → ⊤_bank, GCash (platform) → ⊤_priv. Identical structural form (5 places + 2 invisible, 5 transitions), but invisible-layer caps differ permanently."
